+# Roadmap
+
+Recorded 2026-10-28. Overdue fines and member accounts, holds and renewals are
+done (see `SPEC.md`).
+
+## Renewals (done 2026-10-28; built rules in `SPEC.md`)
+
+- Renewing a loan that is already overdue charges the late fine accrued so far
+  as part of the renewal. It is counted exactly as if the copy had been returned
+  on the renewal day: same rates, cap and child exemption.
+- After the renewal, lateness is counted against the new due date.
+- Lateness before a renewal must never just disappear.
+- **Queue blocks renewal** (2026-10-28): while anyone is still WAITING in the
+  queue for a title, its loans can't be renewed. A READY hold on the hold shelf
+  doesn't count, because that member already has their copy.
+- **Paid up only** (2026-10-28): a member whose balance shows anything at all
+  owed when they ask can't renew until they've paid.
+
+## Decisions (settled 2026-10-28)
+
+- **Cap across a renewal** (decided by the library): the total fine for one loan,
+  including what is charged at renewal and at the final return, never exceeds the
+  title's replacement cost.
+- **Renewing while blocked** — *superseded by "Paid up only" above.* It used to
+  say that renewal follows the borrowing bar and is refused with `AccountBlocked`
+  if the balance, plus the fine the renewal would charge, is 10.00 or more. What
+  still stands: a refused renewal changes nothing (no fine is charged and the due
+  date stays the same), and the lateness isn't lost because it is still charged
+  when the copy comes back. Settled: a refused renewal raises `RenewalRefused`.
+- **Pickup time** (library left it to us; built with holds): 7 days from the day
+  the copy is set aside. If that lands on a Sunday, it moves to the Monday, the
+  same way due dates do. The no-show fee is charged once that day has passed
+  without collection.
